#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:427
#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:465
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:429
msgid "Guest authors let you assign a byline to a post without giving the person a WordPress user account or dashboard access. They are stored as a custom post type and can be created from scratch or generated from an existing user."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:430
msgid "Each guest author has a display name, a slug used in the author archive URL, an optional biography, and contact details. Multiple guest authors (and WordPress users) can be assigned as co-authors to the same post."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:437
msgid "Linking accounts"
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:439
msgid "A guest author can be linked to an existing WordPress user. Linking lets editorial staff manage the byline (display name, biography, avatar) without needing the <code>edit_users</code> capability, and keeps the guest author profile separate from the underlying user account."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:440
msgid "Posts assigned to a guest author that is linked to a user are also counted toward that user's post count, so author archives and post-count displays remain accurate."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:441
msgid "You can link or unlink a user from the Linked Account field on the Edit Guest Author screen."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:448
msgid "Bylines"
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:450
msgid "Guest authors appear wherever bylines are shown: on post bylines on the front end, in the Co-Authors meta box on the post edit screen, and on the author archive page using the guest author's slug."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:451
msgid "On the Users screen, the Posts column reflects published posts authored or co-authored by the user (including via a linked guest author), and the Linked Guest Author column shows whether a user has a guest author linked to them."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:467
msgid "This screen edits a single guest author profile. The fields here control how the byline is displayed on the front end and on author archive pages."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:469
msgid "<strong>Display Name</strong> — the name shown in bylines."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:470
msgid "<strong>Slug</strong> — the <code>user_login</code>-equivalent used in the author archive URL. Changing it changes the archive URL."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:471
msgid "<strong>Email, Website</strong> — contact details surfaced in templates that use them."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:472
msgid "<strong>Biographical Info</strong> — long-form description shown by themes that display author bios."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:473
msgid "<strong>Avatar</strong> — uses the featured image of the guest author profile when set, falling back to Gravatar."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:481
#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:1211
#: php/class-coauthors-wp-list-table.php:180
msgid "Linked Account"
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:483
msgid "The Linked Account field associates this guest author with an existing WordPress user. Linking does <em>not</em> overwrite the guest author's display name, biography, or avatar — those remain editable here, independent of the user profile."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:484
msgid "When linked, posts attributed to this guest author also count toward the linked user's published post count, and the user appears in the Linked Guest Author column on the Users screen."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:485
msgid "Linking is useful when migrating historical bylines, or when you want editorial staff to be able to edit a byline without granting the <code>edit_users</code> capability."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:492
msgid "Deleting"
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:494
msgid "When you delete a guest author, you must choose what happens to posts they are bylined on:"
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:496
msgid "<strong>Reassign to another co-author</strong> — replace the deleted byline with another guest author or user."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:497
msgid "<strong>Leave bylines assigned</strong> — keep the existing byline term in place; useful when the guest author still represents historical attribution."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:498
msgid "<strong>Remove byline</strong> — strip this guest author from the posts entirely. If they were the only author, the post falls back to its <code>post_author</code> user."
msgstr ""

#: php/class-coauthors-guest-authors.php:500
msgid "Deleting a guest author does not delete the linked WordPress user (if any)."
msgstr ""

